@startuml
title on_demand and --monitor are orthogonal
skinparam shadowing false
top to bottom direction

rectangle "onedrive process" {
  component "Existing sync engine" as Sync
  component "Remote monitor\nGraph delta / online change" as Remote
  component "Local monitor\ninotify / local reconciliation" as Local
  database "Item DB\nentire eligible online namespace" as DB
  component "FUSE" as Fuse
  folder "Physical files\nhydrated subset only" as Disk
}

cloud "Microsoft OneDrive" as Graph

Graph <--> Remote : all eligible online changes
Remote --> Sync
Sync --> DB : namespace / metadata updates
DB --> Fuse : authoritative presentation
Fuse --> Disk : content I/O only when hydrated
Disk --> Local : local events only for\nphysically resident content
Local --> Sync
Sync --> Graph : existing upload path

note right of Remote
Runs normally with --monitor.
on_demand does not disable or replace it.
end note

note right of Local
Cloud-only files have no physical inode/content
to monitor locally. They remain represented
through remote state + DB + FUSE.
end note
@enduml
